1
00:00:00,630 --> 00:00:02,420
[♪ opening music begins]

2
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:27,710
[♪ opening music ends]

3
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:32,800
[♪ cheerful music]

4
00:01:34,090 --> 00:01:36,180
[soft breathing]

5
00:01:37,510 --> 00:01:40,220
[EMA] Honestly, Lara,
Mari's been at school

6
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:42,520
all day and you haven't
done a single thing.

7
00:01:43,310 --> 00:01:44,650
Huh?

8
00:01:44,770 --> 00:01:47,070
The window you broke
cost Y¥100,000.

9
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:49,030
-Right.
-But you...

10
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:50,650
STRAWBERRY DAIFUKU

11
00:01:51,030 --> 00:01:52,490
See, I told you they were good.

12
00:01:52,610 --> 00:01:54,610
OCEAN CREATURES
OCEAN ENCYCLOPEDIA

13
00:01:57,450 --> 00:01:59,540
We work hard here.
That's our rule.

14
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:02,040
Rule? I didn't know
there were rules.

15
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:05,420
[EMA] There are now.
Mari, that includes you too.

16
00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:08,880
You said you wanted
money for some Airheads?

17
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,130
-[MARI] AirPods Pro.
-Isn't that what you have?

18
00:02:11,470 --> 00:02:13,260
They're old.
I need a new pair.

19
00:02:13,510 --> 00:02:15,260
I can't keep up.
If you want them,

20
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:16,800
get a job and earn the money.

21
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:21,220
But I don't even know if getting
a job is something I can do.

22
00:02:21,350 --> 00:02:22,560
It's not all bad, you know.

23
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:26,230
I actually met my wife while
I was working at a job.

24
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:27,520
Really?

25
00:02:28,060 --> 00:02:29,940
So then I might meet
my prince at a job?

26
00:02:30,230 --> 00:02:32,280
Hmm... maybe?

27
00:02:32,990 --> 00:02:35,110
[gasps] I'll do it!

28
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:37,240
I'm going to go to work!

29
00:02:38,990 --> 00:02:40,580
You wrote until
pretty late, huh?

30
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:43,120
[MARI] It was her first
time writing by hand,

31
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:45,960
so I stayed up all night
to make it look good.

32
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:48,420
Well, it's good to prepare
yourself for the day.

33
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:52,380
Although, the real
work starts now.

34
00:02:54,470 --> 00:02:56,510
I'm Mari Otsu.
I'm a high school student.

35
00:02:57,550 --> 00:03:00,430
My name is Lara. I'm a princess
of the royal family.

36
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:03,140
I can only work once a week
'cause I prioritize boxing.

37
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:06,650
Have I ever worked before?
No, not at all!

38
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:09,650
The higher hourly wage can be,
the better it is for me.

39
00:03:10,310 --> 00:03:11,440
What am I good at?

40
00:03:12,110 --> 00:03:14,610
Well, I'm great at
telling starfish apart.

41
00:03:16,910 --> 00:03:17,610
[both sigh]

42
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:21,620
I wonder if everyone just does
not want me to work for them.

43
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:23,580
I was sure I was
going to get the job.

44
00:03:23,950 --> 00:03:24,710
[both sigh]

45
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:28,130
Don't worry, girls.
You should just keep applying.

46
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:30,130
Plenty of jobs out there.

47
00:03:30,540 --> 00:03:32,550
There's sure to be something
perfect for both.

48
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:33,710
Just you wait.

49
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:38,130
Oh, by the way, Mr. Makoto,
what do you do for work?

50
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:40,680
Mari, show her my camera.

51
00:03:46,350 --> 00:03:48,150
That is my work gear.

52
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:49,520
This is your job?

53
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:51,610
It's a job where I
press that button.

54
00:03:51,980 --> 00:03:53,530
Huh?! No way!

55
00:03:54,030 --> 00:03:55,530
Is there really a job that easy?

56
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:57,780
Lara, why not give it a go?

57
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:01,160
-This one's a little bit easier.
-Huh?

58
00:04:03,370 --> 00:04:04,370
[Lara sighs]

59
00:04:04,910 --> 00:04:07,410
You won't make any money
seeing as you're not a pro.

60
00:04:08,250 --> 00:04:10,250
But press the shutter
and you can capture

61
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:11,710
any scene right in front of you.

62
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:14,340
Mess up, and
you can't delete it

63
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:15,670
like on a smartphone.

64
00:04:16,510 --> 00:04:18,760
-See what you can capture.
-Wow.

65
00:04:21,050 --> 00:04:21,970
[sighs]

66
00:04:22,350 --> 00:04:23,890
Ah! A castle?

67
00:04:24,220 --> 00:04:25,930
I'm pretty sure that's
a cake shop.

68
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,180
Cake?

69
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:29,640
I'd love to make
a cake sometime,

70
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:33,480
especially... in
a place this lovely.

71
00:04:34,070 --> 00:04:36,110
I might even meet
my prince there.

72
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:37,610
OFFICE

73
00:04:37,740 --> 00:04:40,110
[MANAGER] Oh, you
applied together?

74
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,360
[BOTH] Yes.

75
00:04:42,370 --> 00:04:44,660
You're certainly keen.
Why did you apply?

76
00:04:45,830 --> 00:04:49,040
I applied because I love
sweets and cake, and I'll work

77
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:50,290
harder than anyone else!

78
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:53,130
Hmm, but there are a
lot of kids like you

79
00:04:53,250 --> 00:04:55,250
who just quit as soon
as they get bored.

80
00:04:56,130 --> 00:04:57,670
Any part-time experience?

81
00:04:58,380 --> 00:05:01,260
Well, the thing is, I've never
passed an interview before.

82
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:03,260
Huh? How many did you apply for?

83
00:05:03,390 --> 00:05:04,970
I think about 20.

84
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:06,010
20?

85
00:05:06,510 --> 00:05:08,980
If you apply many times,
you usually get hired.

86
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:12,900
Especially if you say you're
the hardest-working

87
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:14,230
person in the world.

88
00:05:16,980 --> 00:05:18,280
Oh, right!

89
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:20,690
Your kingdom-— um,
I mean company!

90
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:24,450
I really resonate with your
company's founding philosophy.

91
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:27,410
Either way, my strength is that
I never give up.

92
00:05:27,830 --> 00:05:30,040
So my weakness is that I'm
kind of stubborn.

93
00:05:31,370 --> 00:05:34,170
And if I had to describe myself,
I'm like a dried squid.

94
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:37,630
A bit rough around
the edges, but I, I...

95
00:05:38,170 --> 00:05:40,510
[gasp]
I would...

96
00:05:41,470 --> 00:05:43,430
absolutely die for cake!

97
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:45,470
[Lara breathing heavily]

98
00:05:46,350 --> 00:05:48,470
-And you?
-I wouldn't die for cake.

99
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,520
Right.

100
00:05:52,190 --> 00:05:54,350
Hi! Nice to meet you both.

101
00:05:54,770 --> 00:05:56,940
Mari, you'll be
on the sales floor with me.

102
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:59,150
-Lara, you'll be in the kitchen.
-[BOTH] Okay.

103
00:05:59,690 --> 00:06:01,190
Your lockers are over there.

104
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:03,610
LARA

105
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:07,450
Hey, Mari,
what does this say here?

106
00:06:08,450 --> 00:06:10,160
-Says, I'd die for cake.
-Huh?

107
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,870
[background chatter]

108
00:06:13,170 --> 00:06:15,130
[♪ cheerful music playing]

109
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:19,550
[LARA] Wow!

110
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:22,420
Uh...

111
00:06:22,550 --> 00:06:24,090
I can't believe I actually
get to make a cake!

112
00:06:25,010 --> 00:06:27,300
Hey, Mari, come
over here, new girl.

113
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:32,310
-We'll start with washing up.
-Don't I get to make any cake?

114
00:06:32,810 --> 00:06:35,640
Washing up is an important
step in the cake-making process.

115
00:06:36,650 --> 00:06:39,520
Right, I see.
I'll do my best!

116
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:42,570
[grunts]

117
00:06:45,030 --> 00:06:46,160
[grunts]

118
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:50,330
[grunts intensify]

119
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:53,660
There's still more
washing up to do.

120
00:06:55,330 --> 00:06:57,380
-Mr. Manager?
-Yes, what?

121
00:06:57,500 --> 00:07:00,000
I'd really like to start
making cakes soon, please.

122
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,590
Told you that washing up is
an important job, right?

123
00:07:03,170 --> 00:07:05,880
Yes, you did,
but this is exhausting.

124
00:07:06,010 --> 00:07:08,180
That's right,
that's what hard work is.

125
00:07:09,010 --> 00:07:10,350
Work is basically torture.

126
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:14,350
Sorry about that. Manager's
a bit strict, isn't he?

127
00:07:14,890 --> 00:07:15,730
It's torture.

128
00:07:17,140 --> 00:07:19,270
Looks like the washing's
piling up again.

129
00:07:20,150 --> 00:07:21,820
Let's do our best.
Come on, Lara.

130
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:23,400
[wails]

131
00:07:23,530 --> 00:07:25,690
[cash register rings]

132
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:28,030
[sighs]

133
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:33,250
[LARA] Just what is it
I'm trying to do exactly?

134
00:07:33,370 --> 00:07:36,330
[WITCH] Indeed, you mustn't
forget the reason you're here.

135
00:07:36,830 --> 00:07:39,380
But do you think you'll find
the prince there?

136
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:42,550
[ominous tone]

137
00:07:44,550 --> 00:07:46,340
You know, I'm not really sure.

138
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:49,260
It could be a
customer in the shop.

139
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:50,720
Huh?

140
00:07:51,930 --> 00:07:52,760
Or maybe not.

141
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:54,890
ANDEKEN

142
00:07:55,020 --> 00:07:57,190
Good morning.
I was wondering-—

143
00:07:57,520 --> 00:07:58,560
Shh.

144
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:03,070
[magical chime]

145
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:04,940
[gasps]

146
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:08,950
Wow, it's delicious!

147
00:08:09,070 --> 00:08:10,030
You're a genius!

148
00:08:11,450 --> 00:08:13,490
-Mr. Manager?
-Huh?

149
00:08:13,990 --> 00:08:15,910
I would like to make a
cake soon, please.

150
00:08:16,580 --> 00:08:18,500
You're the only one
having fun here.

151
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:19,670
Huh, you sure?

152
00:08:20,210 --> 00:08:22,580
You said that work is
going to be torture.

153
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:25,960
Hmm. You know,
work isn't torture.

154
00:08:26,090 --> 00:08:28,430
It's actually quite fun.
Today, at least.

155
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:29,590
Today?

156
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:32,300
If you want to help
out, I'll let you.

157
00:08:32,930 --> 00:08:34,350
-[Lara sighs]
-Really?

158
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:37,020
You've got your work
cut out for you now.

159
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:39,940
Stick with me until the new
product is finished.

160
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:41,310
-Are you ready?
-[wails]

161
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,400
[♪ upbeat music]

162
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:44,610
Alright, we're making
a peach tart.

163
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:50,070
YAMANASHI PEACH
DAICHI FARMS

164
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:52,700
Yes, peel this one.

165
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:55,330
[♪ upbeat music]

166
00:08:55,990 --> 00:08:57,040
[grunts]

167
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:00,370
[grunts]

168
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:02,290
Actually, peel this one instead.

169
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:09,170
The cream's proportions are key.

170
00:09:13,050 --> 00:09:14,140
Hmm, it's not right.

171
00:09:20,180 --> 00:09:21,390
Still not right.

172
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:28,440
Hey, Lara, make sure you don't
get any shells in there.

173
00:09:31,650 --> 00:09:34,450
Lara, can you start preparing
the sponge cake, please?

174
00:09:37,830 --> 00:09:38,660
Lara?

175
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:42,160
Lara?

176
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:46,460
Lara!

177
00:09:55,430 --> 00:09:57,300
ANDEKEN

178
00:09:58,010 --> 00:10:00,390
[magic sound]
[workers cheer and applaud]

179
00:10:01,310 --> 00:10:02,810
It's too early to celebrate.

180
00:10:02,930 --> 00:10:04,560
We've gotta get
this product ready.

181
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:08,270
Hey, Lara, let's get to peeling!

182
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:09,610
Yes, right!

183
00:10:13,110 --> 00:10:16,660
-Good work today.
-Yeah, we all worked hard.

184
00:10:17,030 --> 00:10:18,080
See you later.

185
00:10:26,250 --> 00:10:27,210
Thanks for today.

186
00:10:33,130 --> 00:10:35,630
You've been a big help.
You worked hard today.

187
00:10:36,050 --> 00:10:37,260
Be proud of yourself.

188
00:10:42,890 --> 00:10:45,140
[♪ soft piano music]

189
00:10:47,230 --> 00:10:48,230
[cat meows]

190
00:10:52,610 --> 00:10:56,410
I wonder how many days
I've been working now.

191
00:10:58,280 --> 00:11:01,330
I mustn't forget that I really
need to find true love soon.

192
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:04,210
[♪ soft piano music]

193
00:11:04,910 --> 00:11:07,500
Big sis, I don't understand.

194
00:11:08,170 --> 00:11:09,630
Why won't you come to see me?

195
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:14,470
Lady Lisa, aren't you
going to see her?

196
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:20,430
[♪ soft piano music]

197
00:11:20,550 --> 00:11:21,390
Lara...

198
00:11:21,510 --> 00:11:22,560
[car starts]

199
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:25,020
I promise... I'll protect you.

200
00:11:25,230 --> 00:11:27,520
[magic sound]

201
00:11:32,070 --> 00:11:34,780
[♪ soft piano music]

202
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:43,620
I seriously can't just
keep working like this.

203
00:11:44,410 --> 00:11:46,660
It needs to end, and soon.

204
00:11:47,670 --> 00:11:49,580
Mr. Manager, can you tell me

205
00:11:49,710 --> 00:11:51,420
how much I'm getting
paid this month?

206
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:53,130
Well, I'm not sure.

207
00:11:53,250 --> 00:11:55,300
It's probably around Y¥70,000.

208
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:56,470
70,000?

209
00:11:57,550 --> 00:12:00,140
Ema told me
to earn Y¥100,000, so...

210
00:12:01,180 --> 00:12:02,890
Well, first, focus on doing the

211
00:12:03,010 --> 00:12:04,520
work in front of you correctly.

212
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:06,980
Once you've improved
step by step, and

213
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:09,350
when you're able to handle
bigger jobs with ease,

214
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:10,770
then I'll raise your wage.

215
00:12:12,020 --> 00:12:13,940
I have to do bigger jobs?

216
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:17,650
Whoa, Lara, you're not ready
for the oven just yet.

217
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:21,240
Oh, but please, I need to
do the big jobs.

218
00:12:21,450 --> 00:12:22,530
Huh?

219
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:25,160
Hey, I've seen this before.

220
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,870
You press this
button here, right?

221
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:29,580
Whoa, no!

222
00:12:30,790 --> 00:12:33,290
If you press it at the wrong
time, it'll ruin everything.

223
00:12:33,590 --> 00:12:35,460
You absolutely
must not touch it.

224
00:12:38,590 --> 00:12:41,130
Hey, please, can you teach me
how to do your job?

225
00:12:41,970 --> 00:12:43,680
Not right now.
Next time.

226
00:12:44,850 --> 00:12:47,430
Lara, come on, you need
to peel these peaches.

227
00:12:48,230 --> 00:12:50,350
[♪ lighthearted piano music]

228
00:12:59,070 --> 00:13:01,070
I really can't keep
going like this.

229
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:03,950
[♪ lighthearted piano music]

230
00:13:04,530 --> 00:13:08,000
But I guess...
I have no choice.

231
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:11,160
[oven timer beeps]

232
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,670
[sighs]

233
00:13:21,430 --> 00:13:23,390
[oven timer keeps beeping]

234
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:37,730
Why did you touch the button?

235
00:13:38,230 --> 00:13:39,360
I'm sorry!

236
00:13:40,490 --> 00:13:41,990
I thought I had to stop it.

237
00:13:42,530 --> 00:13:44,280
It was just an alarm, you know.

238
00:13:44,530 --> 00:13:45,990
I'll go tell the manager.

239
00:13:46,530 --> 00:13:48,240
I guess he'll be
working late tonight.

240
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:51,540
Oh wait, let me try to take
care of it first.

241
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:53,670
I can make them again,
I know I can.

242
00:13:54,210 --> 00:13:55,340
Lara, wait.

243
00:13:56,130 --> 00:13:57,670
I'm partly to blame for this.

244
00:13:57,800 --> 00:14:00,340
Just support me like you
always do. That's all I need.

245
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:07,550
OFFICE

246
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:10,140
I don't want to add more
stress to your life...

247
00:14:11,640 --> 00:14:12,730
but what's the rush?

248
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,400
Well?

249
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:21,610
Ema told me I had to
go out and get a job,

250
00:14:22,990 --> 00:14:25,370
and this is the only place
that would hire me.

251
00:14:26,870 --> 00:14:30,370
But I've lost sight of why I'm
working here in the first place.

252
00:14:32,040 --> 00:14:33,500
I'm supposed to be out there.

253
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:35,670
Trying to find my prince.

254
00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:40,130
It's okay if you want to quit.
There's no shame in it.

255
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:45,010
[WITCH] What exactly are you
doing day in and day out?

256
00:14:45,590 --> 00:14:48,800
You haven't forgotten about
your family, have you?

257
00:14:49,930 --> 00:14:51,260
You don't need to worry.

258
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:53,430
Tomorrow I'll tell
them I'm quitting.

259
00:14:55,310 --> 00:14:57,190
Quitting because
you messed up?

260
00:14:58,570 --> 00:15:00,730
-No, that's not it.
-[MARI] Hmm.

261
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:06,280
What about the money? You know
grandma's gonna get mad again.

262
00:15:09,370 --> 00:15:10,410
Either way....

263
00:15:11,370 --> 00:15:13,000
I think you tried your best.

264
00:15:14,160 --> 00:15:16,330
[♪ melancholic piano music]

265
00:15:20,380 --> 00:15:21,960
ANDEKEN

266
00:15:22,090 --> 00:15:24,220
[LARA] Today is my last day.

267
00:15:26,260 --> 00:15:28,430
[♪ piano music continues]

268
00:15:32,260 --> 00:15:35,350
[♪ piano music continues]

269
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:50,450
I'M WILLING TO DIE FOR CAKE!

270
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:52,200
[LARA] Good morning.

271
00:15:52,530 --> 00:15:53,750
Lara! You're early.

272
00:15:54,250 --> 00:15:55,410
Yes! Good morning.

273
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:59,330
Can't go into the kitchen
without changing first.

274
00:15:59,630 --> 00:16:01,040
You'll bring in dust.

275
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:06,920
So, um, Mr. Manager?

276
00:16:07,220 --> 00:16:08,170
What is it?

277
00:16:08,510 --> 00:16:09,590
I- well...

278
00:16:12,050 --> 00:16:13,050
Everyone!

279
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:16,140
I'm so sorry for
causing trouble!

280
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:17,520
Yesterday!

281
00:16:20,150 --> 00:16:22,320
Yeah, it was really tough
after you did that.

282
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,400
-So tough.
-Oh.

283
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:27,280
Don't worry about it.
It happens all the time.

284
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:30,200
In fact, Ishiyama here makes
even worse mistakes.

285
00:16:30,490 --> 00:16:31,950
He always burns things.

286
00:16:32,070 --> 00:16:34,410
Exactly! And you never
mix the cream properly.

287
00:16:34,530 --> 00:16:37,500
-Go change your clothes now.
-Yes.

288
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:41,580
I think we should have a
welcome party very soon.

289
00:16:43,130 --> 00:16:45,460
[EMA] That's plenty for
the window, thanks.

290
00:16:45,590 --> 00:16:47,210
And the rest is all yours.

291
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:48,260
Huh?

292
00:16:48,630 --> 00:16:50,590
Well, you worked hard for it,
didn't you?

293
00:16:51,430 --> 00:16:52,430
[gasps]

294
00:16:53,140 --> 00:16:55,180
With this much money,
I can buy anything I want!

295
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:58,430
Mari! I'll buy you
cocoa every day!

296
00:16:58,560 --> 00:16:59,980
Don't waste your money already.

297
00:17:00,940 --> 00:17:04,020
[♪ soft piano music
and woman singing]

298
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:07,320
[background chatter]

299
00:17:24,540 --> 00:17:26,710
[LARA] So she calls
Mr. Manager Seta?

300
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:30,300
I mean, she's a
senior after all.

301
00:17:31,170 --> 00:17:32,130
How interesting.

302
00:17:35,050 --> 00:17:38,520
So tell me, what's your plan,
huh? You said you were

303
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:39,470
quitting earlier.

304
00:17:39,980 --> 00:17:40,930
Mm-hmm.

305
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:44,360
[LARA] But lately I've been
thinking about something.

306
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:48,360
It's just...

307
00:17:49,990 --> 00:17:53,740
I've been wanting to
know more about you,

308
00:17:54,820 --> 00:17:57,240
about humans,
for a long time now.

309
00:17:59,870 --> 00:18:02,330
Washing dishes and
peeling fruit is hard work,

310
00:18:03,460 --> 00:18:05,420
but the more I get to
know about your world,

311
00:18:06,290 --> 00:18:08,090
the more I see a new
side of you all,

312
00:18:09,090 --> 00:18:11,460
which makes me want to learn
even more about you.

313
00:18:12,840 --> 00:18:15,640
I really like this feeling
because I believe it's going to

314
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:18,680
lead me to the true love that
I've been searching for.

315
00:18:19,470 --> 00:18:20,470
I think so.

316
00:18:22,140 --> 00:18:26,100
Hmm, so does that mean
you're not quitting after all?

317
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:28,690
Yes, for now...

318
00:18:29,860 --> 00:18:30,900
I think I'll stay.

319
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:34,070
[♪ soft piano music
and woman singing]

320
00:18:38,530 --> 00:18:40,740
-[LARA] I'll take 20.
-[WOMAN] Sure thing,

321
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:45,540
Mari...

322
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:48,540
I wonder how many you'll eat.

323
00:18:49,210 --> 00:18:50,300
Lara.

324
00:18:51,840 --> 00:18:52,670
[gasps]

325
00:18:53,170 --> 00:18:54,220
Lisa?!

326
00:18:59,510 --> 00:19:00,600
You have legs.

327
00:19:02,060 --> 00:19:04,430
[LISA] I've wanted to
see you for so long.

328
00:19:06,390 --> 00:19:09,400
All this time I've been waiting
for you to come back to life.

329
00:19:10,270 --> 00:19:11,360
[LARA] But how?

330
00:19:12,190 --> 00:19:14,570
Surely not Lady Witch's potion?

331
00:19:15,610 --> 00:19:17,280
[LISA] I'm sorry, I didn't want

332
00:19:17,410 --> 00:19:19,240
you to see me in
this hideous form.

333
00:19:21,490 --> 00:19:25,580
My beloved Lara, you're such
a special princess.

334
00:19:27,130 --> 00:19:29,420
The only one who will
save us with your light.

335
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:33,090
But why did you take
the potion again?

336
00:19:34,210 --> 00:19:36,260
What on earth made
you do such a thing?

337
00:19:38,090 --> 00:19:39,140
Because I...

338
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:42,640
I want to save our family
and everyone else.

339
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:44,980
But to do that...

340
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:50,060
I need to find a human
partner and fall in love.

341
00:19:50,610 --> 00:19:51,610
[gasps]

342
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:55,740
-The witch told you that?
-What?

343
00:19:56,490 --> 00:19:57,360
Listen, Lara...

344
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:00,700
you should have learned
this lesson 200 years ago.

345
00:20:01,620 --> 00:20:03,240
A mermaid and a human,

346
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:06,160
there's absolutely no way
they can love each other.

347
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:08,080
No way at all.

348
00:20:11,170 --> 00:20:12,710
[ominous tone]

349
00:20:15,670 --> 00:20:16,670
[Lara sobs] But...

350
00:20:18,010 --> 00:20:19,760
things might be
different tomorrow.

351
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:25,680
Sending Kota there was
the right decision.

352
00:20:28,190 --> 00:20:31,060
I will not allow a mermaid
and a human to fall in love.

353
00:20:33,520 --> 00:20:38,150
You don't need any of them,
not that house, nor that girl.

354
00:20:39,030 --> 00:20:40,070
That girl?

355
00:20:41,030 --> 00:20:43,490
[♪ tense music]

356
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:50,170
[pants]

357
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:56,380
[sighs]

358
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:01,840
Everyone!

359
00:21:01,970 --> 00:21:02,970
[magic sound]

360
00:21:03,390 --> 00:21:06,430
[♪ tense music continues]

361
00:21:12,310 --> 00:21:13,150
Mari!

362
00:21:13,270 --> 00:21:14,520
[magic sound]

363
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:17,480
[growling]

364
00:21:17,610 --> 00:21:18,570
[gasps]

365
00:21:19,400 --> 00:21:22,240
[gasps] It's... moving.

366
00:21:26,540 --> 00:21:27,540
Kota!

367
00:21:28,910 --> 00:21:30,040
[tires screeching]

368
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:33,670
[♪ tense music ends]

369
00:21:35,250 --> 00:21:37,380
[♪ closing music begins]

370
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:39,970
TRANSLATION:
SACHIKO TAKAHASHI

371
00:21:40,090 --> 00:21:42,090
TIMING: ANDY ELLIS

372
00:21:42,220 --> 00:21:44,220
EDITING AND TYPESETTING:
ASHLEY BARBOZA

373
00:21:44,350 --> 00:21:46,260
QUALITY CONTROL:
RILEY DALTON

374
00:21:46,390 --> 00:21:48,430
TRANSLATION CHECK:
SRIRAM GURUNATHAN

375
00:23:02,010 --> 00:23:04,220
[♪ closing music ends]

376
00:23:04,630 --> 00:23:07,510
[panting]

377
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:12,520
Mari!

378
00:23:12,970 --> 00:23:15,190
[voices from the TV]

379
00:23:17,810 --> 00:23:20,610
-What's up?
-Hey, welcome back!

380
00:23:21,150 --> 00:23:22,030
Just in time.

381
00:23:22,150 --> 00:23:24,150
Again? Seriously?

382
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:25,490
Hmm?

383
00:23:29,030 --> 00:23:31,160
[crying]

384
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:35,910
I'm so glad.

385
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:37,620
I'm such an idiot.

386
00:23:38,380 --> 00:23:41,210
[LARA] I guess I just
jumped to conclusions.

387
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:44,210
[sirens wailing in distance]

388
00:23:51,600 --> 00:23:55,390
SHIGA

389
00:23:57,690 --> 00:23:59,440
TO BE CONTINUED
